Since,
$\begin{aligned}
& \text { Since, } \lim _{x \rightarrow 1} f(x) \frac{1}{g(x)} \\
& =\lim _{x \rightarrow 1}\left(\frac{a^{x-1}+b^{x-1}}{2}\right)^{\frac{1}{x-1}}
\end{aligned}$
(it is form $1^{\infty}$ )
$\begin{aligned}
& =\mathrm{e}^{\lim _{\mathrm{x} \rightarrow 1}\left(\frac{\mathrm{a}^{\mathrm{a}-1}+\mathrm{b}^{\mathrm{x}-1}}{2}-1\right) \frac{1}{\mathrm{x}-1}}=\mathrm{e}^{\lim _{\mathrm{x} \rightarrow \mathrm{~m}}\left(\frac{\mathrm{a}^{\mathrm{x}-1}-1}{2(\mathrm{x}-1)}+\frac{\mathrm{b}^{\mathrm{x}-1}-1}{2(\mathrm{x}-1)}\right)} \\
& =e^{\left(\frac{1}{2} \ln a+\frac{1}{2} \operatorname{mb} b\right)}=e^{\frac{1}{2} \ln (a b)}=\sqrt{a b}
\end{aligned}$

$\begin{aligned}
& \lim _{x \rightarrow 0} \frac{x}{\sqrt{1-\cos 4 x}}=\lim _{x \rightarrow 0} \frac{2 x}{\sqrt{2}|\sin 2 x|} \times \frac{1}{2} \\
& \text { L.H.L }=-\frac{1}{2 \sqrt{2}} \text { and R.H.L. }=\frac{1}{2 \sqrt{2}} \\
& \because \quad \text { L.H.L } \neq \text { R.H.L. }
\end{aligned}$
So, $\lim _{x \rightarrow 0} f(x)$ is not exist.

Using L'Hospital rule
$\begin{aligned}
& \lim _{x \rightarrow 0} \frac{-a \sin a x+b \sin b x}{-2 x} \\
& \lim _{x \rightarrow 0} \frac{-a^2 \cos a x+b^2 \cos b x}{2} \\
& =\frac{b^2-a^2}{2}
\end{aligned}$

$\begin{aligned}
& \lim _{x \rightarrow 0} \frac{a^x-b^x}{x} \\
& =\lim _{x \rightarrow 0} \frac{a^x \log e^a-b^x \log e^b}{1}
\end{aligned}$
(using L'Hospital's Rule)
$\begin{aligned} & =\log e^a-\log e^b \\ & =\log \left(\frac{a}{b}\right)\end{aligned}$
